Wouldn't that require quite the sizable corpus? That'd be fairly difficult
to collect and were we to try... I'm not aware of many non-technical lojban
texts. Even worse, most of these texts discuss lojban itself; they're very
specialized on top of being technical.

On the other hand, I think it's doable. The English definitions are usually
pretty broad; but the individual Eng words are more focused. The translator
(or lexicographer?) would have to get the gestalt of the set of the
individual Eng definition words, and then find the best equivalent set in
his/her language so that the lojban concept is the same in both languages
(En/other) to _his/her_ mind.


